A||||2||Gokart||Battery cable question?||||5||
Z||000000||Gokart||05-04-2000||07:21 AM||||The marine store on my route said they would have everything prepared for my "battery to front" project, but I ask them when I looked at the two 8 foot long cables what kind of connectors I should use to splice to the existing cables and they told me not to or it'll be a problem waiting to happen!? If I can't do this then how can I keep the two smaller wires coming off the terminals when the wire I bought doesn't have them! Are they both just grounds so all I'll have to do is ground them? Should I strip out all the old cable or is there a way I can connect these new cables to them? TIA!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Greg Piet||05-04-2000||08:22 AM||||Well the wires from the neg terminal should just be grounds...   I think it is necessary that wherever those wires go, there is a GOOD ground connection to those areas.<BR>As far as the positive leads off the battery, you should be able to run wires from the starter motor connection.  I dont think this would affect anything, but there is a possibility that if the lead that powers the ECM is taken from the starter that the starter may cause noise or a surge and hurt your ECM.  I am not sure!||||reg||1
Z||000002||mwbackus||05-04-2000||08:26 AM||||You can get cable ends that clamp on and they have the small wire attached.  But if the new wires already have nice ends on them, you could use a battery tap made for high power stereo amps.  They are like those crimp on screw termial lugs, only they are gold plated and large enough to use between the cable ends and battery terminals (like a large washer). Any good sound shop should have them.<P>     A better idea would be to use the through panel battery connectors <BR>(Part# 710-74145) from Jegs.  If you locate the through panel connectors near where the battery was originally, you could very likely use your existing cables from there.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.jegs.com/images/products/71074145_large.jpg"> <P><BR>Mike B.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by mwbackus (edited 05-04-2000).]||||reg||1
